source: src/core/recall.rs, src/cli/mod.rs
assertion: code-anchored recall reverse lookup from paths/symbols/diff to anchored memories (ADR 0064 / bd-u875s.2 / bd-u875s.3)
schema:
  payload: ee.recall.v1 (under ee.response.v2 data.recall)
  cursor: ee.recall.cursor.v1 (budget continuation lane)
contracts:
  - at least one selector (--path, --symbol, --diff, --diff-staged) is required; an unselected invocation is a usage error (exit 1), never a silent empty result
  - selector families compose as OR with dedup by memory id, keeping the freshest anchor per memory; --kind/--level filter conjunctively BEFORE ranking; --stale keeps only suspect/stale anchors and adds per-item repair hints
  - ranking is deterministic: freshness_multiplier x confidence x level_tilt with a x1.15 kind bonus for failure|risk|anti-pattern; ties break by ascending memory id; same inputs yield byte-identical output
  - --diff/--diff-staged shell out to git READ-ONLY (path extraction only); git failure degrades to recall_git_unavailable (warning) with an empty diff path set and never blocks; option-shaped refs are refused before the shell-out
  - --budget-tokens keeps the longest ranked prefix under budget; truncation reports the governor vocabulary output_truncated_budget (info) with details.droppedCount and details.continuationCursor (ee.recall.cursor.v1)
  - --cursor resumes a budget page sequence; rejected cursors emit cursor_invalid/cursor_stale (low) with an EMPTY page (never a restarted one), so a page sequence cannot duplicate or skip items across writes
  - a smaller budget yields a strict prefix of a larger budget's items (prefix stability)
  - tombstoned memories are excluded at query time regardless of index hygiene
  - markdown format renders a token-tight prepend block: header with kept/total counts, per-item id/anchor/level/kind/freshness line, single-line content preview, provenance per item, repair hints on stale items, trailing degraded codes
  - the declared output-governor truncation point is data.recall.items[] (global --max-output-tokens lane composes on top of --budget-tokens)
  - effect class is read_only_db; recall never writes, never advances generations
degraded_codes:
  - anchor_index_empty
  - anchor_index_stale
  - recall_filtered_empty
  - recall_git_unavailable
  - output_truncated_budget
  - cursor_invalid
  - cursor_stale
evidence:
  - memory_anchor_index (V076 derived table; rebuilt by `ee index rebuild`)
  - docs/schemas/ee.recall.v1.json
  - docs/adr/0064-code-anchored-recall.md
  - tests/recall_cli_golden.rs
  - tests/fixtures/golden/recall/*.golden
